DEMO-GAME-024 acceptance evidence: DB persistence round trip (writeToDB / EntityAutoLoader / createEntityFromDBID)
Date: 2026-11-28  Machine: Linux 192.168.5.188 (engine + DB both local LAN)
Repo: /home/cui/workspaces/kode  Assets: templates/assets/scripts (synced to tests/fixtures/kbengine-demo-assets)

== Environment
Engine: ~/workspaces/kbengine fork binaries (kbe/bin/server), 9 processes + bots.
Boot A (fresh DB): scripts/run-demo-engine.sh start   -> reset_database() DROPs+CREATEs kode_demo (default KBE_DEMO_DB_RESET=1).
Boot B (keep DB):  KBE_DEMO_DB_RESET=0 scripts/run-demo-engine.sh start  (reset_database skipped; the 023/024 data survives).
  ^ 023 finding, re-proven here: plain 'start' always resets the DB; KBE_DEMO_DB_RESET=0 is mandatory for round-trip boots.
Bots: scripts/run-demo-engine.sh bots  -- now pins --cid=8129652375332859701 so account names
  (bot_<cid>_<n>, create_and_login_handler.cpp) are stable across boots.

== DB capture note
The 192.168.5.5 alias on this machine dropped right after the run (connection refused, host still pings);
kode_demo actually lives in the LOCAL MariaDB. Post-stop capture was taken via local socket (sudo mysql).
Row counts and per-row values match the Run B terminal snapshot field-for-field (see terminal state below).

== Sequence
Run A (boot A, fresh DB): 10 bots register+login, reqSelectAvatar('') roster-miss -> reqCreateAvatar x10,
  avatar.writeToDB(_onNewAvatarSaved, 1)  # shouldAutoLoad=1
  anchors: ROSTER REGISTERED=10, REALM UP=14, SECT CHAT=38, SECT JOIN=7, SELECT AVATAR(create branch)=10
Stop (pkill engine binaries). DB kept.
Run B (boot B, kept DB): EntityAutoLoader restores all 10 avatars BEFORE bots connect:
  baseapp.out: "Avatar[2005] created, name=bot2006" x10 (boot-time autoload restore)
  bots login -> reqSelectAvatar('') -> roster present but createEntityFromDBID path superseded by the
  idle-restored-avatar rebind branch -> 10/10 "REBOUND RESTORED AVATAR" with realm/exp/sectId equal to Run A values.
  anchors: REBOUND RESTORED=10, REALM UP=5 (continuation from restored exp), SECT CHAT=2, SECT JOIN=3 (+1 founder)

