Mapping def-type -> mysql column, confirmed by the capture above:
  UINT8  -> tinyint(3) unsigned   (sm_realm, sm_race, sm_path, AVATAR dbid fields)
  UINT16 -> smallint(5) unsigned  (sm_curTitle, sm_curCostume, Talisman sm_itemId)
  UINT32 -> int(10) unsigned      (sm_level, sm_experience, sm_attrs_*, sm_lastLoginTime)
  UINT64 -> bigint(20) unsigned   (sm_partnerDbid, sm_sectId, sm_ownerDbid, child sm_dbid)
  STRING + DatabaseLength 64 -> varchar(64) (sm_name, sm_sectName); no DatabaseLength -> varchar(255) (child sm_name)
  FIXED_DICT -> flattened sm_<prop>_<sub> columns (spiritRoots_metal..earth x5, appearance_faceId..bodyId x5)
  VECTOR3 Position/Direction -> sm_0_position..sm_2_position / sm_0_direction..sm_2_direction (float x3 each)
  ARRAY <of> T -> child table tbl_<Entity>_<prop> (id bigint PK + parentID bigint MUL + one sm_<field> column per T member)
  Persistent=false props absent (tbl_Account has no sm_accountName column: BASE_AND_CLIENT STRING without Persistent)
  engine-added: id bigint PK auto_increment + sm_autoLoad tinyint(4) on every base table and child row

== Engine findings recorded (024 docstring chain)
1. tbl_accountinfos.bindata only carries the registration snapshot (baseapp.cpp:4215
   onQueryAccountCBFromDbmgr -> createDictDataFromPersistentStream); writeToDB child-table properties
   NEVER reach the login path -> Account roster restoration via login blob is impossible.
2. Engine-native restore channel = EntityAutoLoader (entity_autoloader.cpp): writeToDB(cb, 1) sets
   sm_autoLoad, boot re-creates the entities (base, no client) BEFORE onBaseAppReady.
3. Autoloaded avatars __init__ during boot, before the Spaces manager exists -> enterSpace soft-fails;
   rebind must re-issue enterSpace(DEMO_SPACE_INDEX) when cell is None.
4. Stable naming proved impossible on the real machine: bots client entity ids drift every boot
   (id bases flip with app start order: bot3..bot12 vs bot2003..bot2012) and accountName is empty via
   getattr on both the bots client entity and the base-side Proxy. Selection therefore lives server-side:
   empty name = account roster first entry / idle restored avatar; the name is a display face only.
5. createEntityFromDBID callback signature (baseRef, dbid, wasActive), baseRef=None on failure
   (baseapp.cpp:435/1088); writeToDB onSaved = (success, entity) (entity.cpp:1250-1283).

